                <pb facs="0588" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00111 <hi rendition="#superscript">Lic. Wolf,
                        Rudolf/51</hi>/57: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-23T22:00:00+00:00">February 23, 1937—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 23—4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>264. Embassy’s telegram No. 240, February 18, 8 [<hi rendition="#italic">9</hi>]
                    p.m. Consul at Havre reports that the 17 planes which arrived on the steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Waalhaven</hi> have been sold to the Société Française
                    de Transports Aeriens which will instruct what disposition is to be made of
                    them.</p>
                <p>Upon investigation it appears that this company was formed in September last year
                    with a capital of 100,000 francs and that its present manager is Edouard
                    Godillot (see Embassy’s telegram No. 70, January 16, 3 p.m.) with offices in
                    Paris. The firm has a doubtful reputation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
